/-!
# The exterior alternative in original 15.1.28

The moved-module recognition covers both exterior powers with compatible
actor transport. Removing a fixed direct summand preserves the literal
seed stabilizer, its embedded two-core and its original best offender.
`Exterior.Reduction` applies this transport to the actual source quotient.

`Exterior.SourceCoordinates` constructs the full split source coordinates
and the nonzero Sylow-fixed projected seed, for either exterior power.
`Exterior.ModelCore` proves the concrete seed-core exclusion and applies it
to the literal recognized component. No extra exterior premise remains.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith 15.1.28, printed p.1103.
-/
